-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",89,{
[2817]="700379C2\n1\tTalk to Thurferth, Captain of the Guard\tThurferth is near the centre of Woodhurst. Herubrand told you to speak with Thurferth, Captain of the Guard, about the two men posted at the Mead Hall and whether they have seen anything unusual.\n2\tThurferth suggested other guards posted around the city may be able to help.\t\n3\tTalk to Thurferth, Captain of the Guard\tThurferth is near the centre of Woodhurst. You should tell Thurferth of what you learned from the guards around town.\n",
[2818]="70040E84\n1\tTake the last rowboat to the tall ships\tThe tall ships off the beach of Hashadîr can be reached by taking the last rowboat. You should take the last rowboat to the tall ships.\n2\tDestroy treasure chests (total: 7)\030Burn pitch (total: 5)\tBarrels of pitch and treasure-chests can be found on the tall ships of the Corsairs off the beach of Hashadîr. You should burn the pitch and destroy the treasure chests.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have created a great deal of havoc on the tall ships of the Corsairs anchored off of Hashadîr.\n",
[2819]="70067536\n1\tSpeak with Zarai the Ledger-keeper in Jax Phânal\tZarai offered to provide you with details about the ledger-keepers. Listen to her tale to learn why this organization exists.\n",
[2820]="700684E1\n1\tSpeak with Harthabor\tHarthabor is need of assistance to contact his leader in Umbar Baharbêl. Speak with him to learn more.\n2\tPick up a scrap of meat from the plaza near the sea-hawk\tThe sea-hawk sits atop a roof through the archway and east of Harthabor in Jax Phanâl. Find a method to draw the bird down, collect its message, and return it to the agent.\n3\tPlace the scrap of meat on the flat stone to the north-east\tThe flat stone on the rampart to the north-east may prove a suitable place to lure the sea-hawk from its perch.\n4\tRetrieve the message from the sea-hawk\tYou drew the bird down from its perch and should now remove the message from its leg.\n5\tDeliver the message to Harthabor at Jax Phanâl\tHarthabor is waiting to see the message you retrieved.\n6\tAttach the message to the sea-hawk courier\tThe Watcher on the Wing waits dutifully for you to give it a message to bring back to Achardis. Bring the note and tie it to her leg so she may return it to the Order of the Eagle's leader in Umbar Baharbêl.\n7\tTalk to Harthabor\tThe bird is away. Harthabor awaits your return in Jax Phanâl. Go to the agent and inform him that all went well.\n",
[2821]="700649B8\n1\tTravel to the entrance of Imloth Melui in King's Gondor\tAccording to Pethanar, the gossipmonger of Linhir, King Elessar's travelling party will have reached Imloth Melui by now.\n2\tTalk to Legolas at the entrance to Imloth Melui\030Talk to Gimli at the entrance to Imloth Melui\tLegolas and Gimli have come with King Elessar's travelling party to Imloth Melui.\n3\tTalk to King Elessar inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui\tKing Elessar is inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.\n4\tFind King Elessar's trusted bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos\tKing Elessar told you to find his trusted bodyguard somewhere outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.\n5\tTalk to King Elessar's most trusted bodyguard\tKing Elessar's most trusted bodyguard greets you with a warm smile.\n6\tTalk to Líniel outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui\tLíniel is outside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui.\n",
[2822]="700645A7\n1\tTalk to Glindor in Minas Tirith (Midsummer) and go with him to see King Elessar\tGlindor, King Elessar's herald, is outside the stables in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\n2\tTalk to Gimli north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor\tGimli is north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Legolas north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor\tLegolas is north-east of the Harlond, in King's Gondor.\n",
[2823]="70048BBB\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir just inside the ruin of the Black Gate\tMithrandir asked to meet you just inside the ruin of the Black Gate, there to take the measure of the adventurers that desire to press forward into the land of Mordor.\n2\tTalk to Annoth in Cirith Gorgor\030Talk to Harthalín in Cirith Gorgor\030Talk to Covadil in Cirith Gorgor\030Talk to Rhogrin in Cirith Gorgor\tAdventurers have passed through the ruins of the Black Gate into Cirith Gorgor, and intend to seek treasure and glory in Mordor. Mithrandir asked you to speak to them and warn them against taking brash action.\n3\tDefeat foes in Udûn (total: 8)\tDangerous foes stalk the vale of Udûn, and Mithrandir asked you to venture forth with caution and defeat them.\n4\tSearch Udûn for the forges of Mornaur\tThe forges of Mornaur are on the western side of the vale of Udûn.\n5\tTalk to Rhogrin at Mornaur, in western Udûn\tRhogrin has come to Mornaur, in western Udûn.\n6\tRender anvils at Mornaur difficult to use (total: 5)\tRhogrin asked you to push over some of the anvils at Mornaur, rendering them difficult for the Orcs to use.\n7\tTalk to Rhogrin at Mornaur, in western Udûn\tRhogrin is at Mornaur, in western Udûn.\n8\tDefeat foes in Udûn while you examine enemy movements (total: 6)\030Search the basin where the group of Orcs travelled, north-east of Durthang\tFrom the cliff's edge below Mornaur, Rhogrin saw a large group of Orcs and trolls in the basin of the vale north-east of Durthang, and asked you to investigate in order to make the area safe for other soldiers of Gondor.\n9\tTalk to Rhogrin at Mornaur, in western Udûn\tRhogrin is at Mornaur, in western Udûn.\n",
[2824]="70056E66\n1\tTalk to Kóvo of the Stout-axes in Skarháld\030Talk to Bórnek of the Zhélruka in Skarháld\030Talk to Glóin of the Longbeards in Skarháld\tDurin asked you to climb the stairs at Skarháld in search of Longbeards, Zhélruka, and Stout-axes who might share their opinions on what he should do for them.\n2\tTalk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tDurin is on the lowest level of Skarháld, near the stable-master, waiting for your report from the three dwarf-clans who inhabit the mountain fortress.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin Stonehelm in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor\tDurin's father, King Thorin Stonehelm, is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain in Erebor.\n",
[2825]="70048C05\n1\tFind Annoth outside Durthand, once the fortress of the Thandrim\tAnnoth went to the fortress of Durthand, in Udûn, and has not returned.\n2\tTalk to Annoth outside Durthand, once the fortress of the Thandrim\tAnnoth is outside the fortress that once belonged to the Thandrim, and was called Durthand.\n3\tTalk to Annoth outside Durthang and listen to his tale of the Thandrim\tAnnoth is outside the fortress that once belonged to the Thandrim, and was called Durthand.\n4\tTalk to Annoth outside Durthang\tAnnoth is outside the fortress of Durthang, in southern Udûn.\n",
[2826]="700645A9\n1\tTalk to Othanar inside the Harlond\tLegolas suggested that someone to the south-west must be overseeing the repairs of the Harlond.\n2\tClean up rubble piles inside the Harlond (total: 6)\030Collect wooden planks in the Harlond (total: 6)\030Defeat rats throughout the Harlond (total: 6)\tOthanar asked you to clean up rubble piles, collect wooden planks, and defeat the rats that now infest the Harlond.\n3\tBring the wooden planks to Othanar in the Harlond\tOthanar oversees the rebuilding of the Harlond by the north-eastern entrance.\n4\tTalk to Legolas in the Harlond\tLegolas is working along the docks south-east of Othanar in the Harlond.\n5\tTalk to Gimli in the Harlond\tGimli is in the Harlond, helping Legolas with the rebuilding effort.\n6\tApproach the small crowd and listen to their conversation\tA small crowd of Gondorians speaks in hushed tones to the east of Legolas and Gimli. You should get closer to them and listen to their conversation.\n7\tTalk to Berthon in the Harlond\tBerthon speaks to a small crowd of Gondorians by the docks of the Harlond.\n8\tTalk to Legolas in the Harlond\tLegolas stands to the west of the whispering Gondorians by the docks of the Harlond.\n",
[2827]="70056E67\n1\tFind Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor\tKing Thorin Stonehelm has tasked you with going to Nabgûn-mazaru, the home of Stáli the Hewer, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, and asking him about 'the Greymauls.'\n2\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer in Nabgûn-mazaru\tStáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown, lives at Nabgûn-mazaru, south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n3\tExamine the mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog\tStáli the Hewer has been restoring a mosaic depicting the death of Mótsog and the end of the Greymaul Rebellion, and he has invited you to admire it. The mosaic is currently in his workshop of Nabgûn-mazaru, but it will be returned to the hall where it came from once his work is finished.\n4\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer in Nabgûn-mazaru\tStáli the Hewer, a Longbeard artist and sculptor of some renown, lives south-west of the entrance to the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n",
[2828]="70056E68\n1\tExamine the statue of Durin the Deathless carved by Stáli the Hewer\tStáli the Hewer has invited you to look at the statue he carved of Durin the Deathless, located in his home and workshop of Nabgûn-mazaru.\n2\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer in Nabgûn-mazaru\tStáli the Hewer is in Nabgûn-mazaru, his workshop and home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor\tKing Thorin is in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.\n",
[2829]="700645C9\n1\tTravel to the village of Arnach, south-west of the Harlond, in King's Gondor\tLegolas believes the three of you should investigate these rumours in the village of Arnach, to the south-west.\n2\tTalk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach\tBaranor stands in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n3\tDefeat wild beasts and other foes of Arnach throughout Lossarnach, in King's Gondor (total: 8)\tWild beasts and other dangers to Arnach can be found throughout Lossarnach.\n4\tTalk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach\tBaranor stands in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n5\tSearch for some sign of Balakhôr by the shore south of Arnach, in King's Gondor\tAccording to Baranor, some folk of Arnach believe Balakhôr survived the fighting at Pelargir and came ashore south of Arnach.\n6\tExamine the abandoned camp-fire\030Examine the bag of dirty clothes\030Examine the boat among the reeds not far from the camp-fire\tYou found the remnants of an old camp... but how old is it, and who made it?\n7\tTalk to Gimli by the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach\tGimli has joined you by the camp-fire south of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n8\tTalk to Legolas by the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach\tLegolas stands deep in thought near the abandoned camp-fire south of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n",
[2830]="70048C06\n1\tDefeat Orc-kind inside Durthang (total: 8)\tThe fortress of Durthang is in southern Udûn.\n2\tUse Cell Door (total: 2)\tThe dungeon of Durthang is in the south-eastern corner of the fortress.\n3\tThe dungeon of Durthang is in the south-eastern corner of the fortress.\t\n4\tTalk to Annoth in the dungeon of Durthang\tYou have freed a number of prisoners from their cells in the dungeon of Durthang.\n5\tFind Ayorzén in the north-eastern section of Durthang\tAyorzén fled from the dungeon, but he headed deeper into the fortress of Durthang. Where is he going? Annoth volunteered to search the western side of the fortress, which leaves the north-eastern corner for you.\n6\tTalk to the Vault-guard\tThe guard of the vault of Durthang was attacked by Ayorzén when the Easterling escaped.\n7\tTalk to Annoth outside Durthang\tAnnoth is outside the fortress of Durthang, in southern Udûn.\n",
[2831]="70048C32\n1\tFind the Isenmouthe, the gate between Udûn and Dor Amarth\tAnnoth believes Ayorzén will try to pass through the Isenmouthe, the gate in Carach Angren that bars passage between Udûn and Dor Amarth.\n2\tMany foes hold the gate of Isenmouthe.\t\n3\tMany foes hold the Isenmouthe.\t\n4\tShow the message you recovered to Annoth near the Isenmouthe (The message can be read from your inventory)\tAnnoth has come to the Isenmouthe in search of Ayorzén.\n5\tDefeat Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn, in Udûn ([see journal]/6)\tAyorzén may have gone to Rhûd Vorn, an Easterling camp in Udûn. You should defeat its warriors while you search for him.\n6\tDefeat Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn, in Udûn (5/6)\tYou should search the Easterling camp of Rhûd Vorn for any sign of Ayorzén.\n7\tFind Annoth along the road south of Rhûd Vorn\tAnnoth was going to follow you to the Easterling camp. Walk down the slope south of the Easterling camp and tell him there was no sign of Ayorzén.\n8\tTalk to Ayorzén the Wily by the side of the road in Udûn\tYou have found Ayorzén. He is sitting with his back against a rock by the side of the road, south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn.\n9\tTalk to Annoth by the road south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn\tAnnoth is south of the Easterling encampment in Udûn, where Ayorzén waited for you.\n10\tBring the corrupted heirloom to Mithrandir, just inside the ruined Black Gate\tMithrandir is just inside the ruined Black Gate, in Cirith Gorgor.\n",
[2832]="70056E91\n1\tTalk to Agnar Brokentooth and measure his combat prowess\030Talk to Lági Helmbiter and measure his combat prowess\030Talk to Reithvald Red-ember and measure his combat prowess\tKing Thorin Stonehelm asked you to test the combat readiness of three survivors of the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, which occurred more than two hundred and twenty years ago. These three heroes can be found in the passages leading to the Dwelling-halls and the New-lodes, in Erebor.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor\tKing Thorin Stonehelm is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.\n",
[2833]="70064620\n1\tTalk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach\tBaranor is the Captain of the Guardsmen of Arnach, north of the abandoned camp-site in King's Gondor.\n2\tTravel to the Crossings of Erui, south-west of Arnach, in King's Gondor\tThe Crossings of Erui are located to the south-west of the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Glassiel at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor\tAt the Crossings of Erui you encountered the woman Glassiel, floating baskets on the river.\n4\tListen to Glassiel speak of the Five Sisters\tGlassiel speaks to you of the Five Sisters of Lebennin.\n5\tListen to Glassiel speak of the Five Sisters\tGlassiel speaks to you of the Five Sisters of Lebennin.\n6\tListen to Glassiel speak of the Five Sisters\tGlassiel speaks to you of the Five Sisters of Lebennin.\n7\tListen to Glassiel speak of the Five Sisters\tGlassiel speaks to you of the Five Sisters of Lebennin.\n8\tTalk to Glassiel at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor\tGlassiel speaks to you of the Five Sisters of Lebennin.\n9\tTalk to Gimli at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor\tGimli stands at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.\n10\tTalk to Legolas at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor\tLegolas stands at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.\n11\tTalk to Glassiel at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor\tGlassiel is at the Crossings of Erui, in King's Gondor.\n12\tDefeat foes on the way to Halach, in King's Gondor (total: 6)\tYou agreed to aid the folk of Lebennin by defeating foes between the Crossings of Erui and Halach.\n13\tTravel to the town of Halach in King's Gondor\tYou agreed to make safe the lands between the Crossings of Erui and Glassiel's home of Halach, in King's Gondor. Now you should ensure she arrived safely.\n14\tTalk to Glassiel in her home-town of Halach\tGlassiel stands inside the entrance to Halach.\n15\tTalk to Breglang in Halach\tBreglang, a sailor at Halach, has called for your attention.\n16\tRetrieve fishing nets from near the docks of Halach (total: 4)\030Collect building supply crates within Halach (total: 2)\tFishing nets can be drawn in along the docks of Halach.\n17\tReturn to Breglang in the town of Halach, in King's Gondor\tBreglang is in the town of Halach, waiting for you to return from your errands.\n18\tTravel to the town of Glaniath, north-west of Halach in King's Gondor\tIt is time for you to meet up with Legolas and Gimli in the town of Glaniath, to the north-west.\n19\tTalk to Legolas by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor\tLegolas sits on a bench by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor.\n",
[2834]="70056E95\n1\tReturn to Skarháld with the Longbeard force\tKing Thorin has asked you to return to Skarháld with the great force of Longbeards he commanded to reinforce his son Durin.\n2\tTalk to Mírkuz at Skarháld\tMírkuz eyes the Longbeard force with great suspicion.\n3\tTalk to Glóin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tGlóin stands near the stable-master at Skarháld, pleased to see the Longbeard reinforcements from the Lonely Mountain.\n4\tTalk to Glóin and go with him to search for Durin\tGlóin stands near the stable-master at Skarháld. He is worried that Durin left the fortress some time ago and has not returned.\n5\tTalk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tDurin has returned to Skarháld with renewed purpose, his eyes alight with hopeful flame.\n",
[2835]="70048C37\n1\tFind the foundries of Anglach\tThe foundries and mines of Anglach are in north-eastern Udûn.\n2\tAdventurers affected by the choking fumes can be found at the foundries of Anglach, in north-eastern Udûn.\t\n3\tTalk to Belaith at Anglach\tBelaith leads a group of adventurers seeking treasure in at Anglach, in Udûn.\n4\tDefeat Orcs in the mines below Anglach and retrieve treasure (total: 6)\tBelaith asked you to delve into the mines below Anglach in search of treasure and refused to return to the Black Gate with his men until you have brought him some.\n5\tBring the treasure you collected to Belaith, at Anglach\tBelaith leads a group of adventurers seeking treasure in at Anglach, in Udûn.\n6\tTalk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is outside the Black Gate.\n7\tTalk to Ayorzén outside the Black Gate\tAyorzén sits near Mithrandir outside the Black Gate.\n8\tTalk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is outside the Black Gate.\n",
[2836]="7006462F\n1\tTalk to Arvellon in the centre of Glaniath, in King's Gondor\tArvellon is in the centre of Glaniath, and Legolas believes you should speak with him.\n2\tCollection boxes can be found beside stone buildings on the outskirts of Glaniath. Arvellon asked you to gather the tokens cast by townspeople of Glaniath in support of his proposal.\t\n3\tTalk to Arvellon in the centre of Glaniath, in King's Gondor\tArvellon is in the centre of Glaniath, waiting for you to return with the tokens cast in support of his proposal.\n4\tTalk to Gimli by the entrance to Glaniath, in King's Gondor\tGimli is by the entrance to Glaniath.\n5\tTravel to the eastern entrance of Pelargir, south-west of Glaniath, in King's Gondor\tThe port city of Pelargir is to the south-west of Glaniath, in King's Gondor.\n6\tTalk to Captain Thandor by the eastern entrance to Pelargir\tCaptain Thandor is in the square by the eastern entrance to Pelargir, in King's Gondor.\n7\tEnter Sirgon's Manor in Pelargir and find its lord\tSirgon's Manor is located down the street to the west of the north-east entrance of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.\n8\tTalk to Sirgon in his manor\tSirgon rests on a bench inside the entrance to his manor.\n9\tWait for Sirgon to speak\tSirgon rests on a bench inside his manor, thinking about the tidings you brought to him.\n10\tTalk to Sirgon inside his manor\tSirgon has come to a decision, and is ready to speak with you.\n11\tMeet Sirgon in his room of keepsakes, to the north\tSirgon has asked to meet you in his room of keepsakes, to the north, where he will speak with you further.\n12\tTalk to Sirgon in his room of keepsakes\tSirgon stands in his room of keepsakes, appraising his treasured memories.\n13\tSirgon has suggested that you examine the keepsakes he acquired over a long life at sea.\t\n14\tTalk to Sirgon inside his room of keepsakes\tSirgon considers the treasured memories in his room of keepsakes.\n15\tTalk to Faltharan inside Sirgon's room of keepsakes\tFaltharan stands within his father's room of keepsakes.\n",
[2837]="70056E94\n1\tCollect weapons from the western armoury up the stairs inside the Skarháld keep\tThe western armoury is up the stairs inside the Skarháld keep.\n2\tCollect weapons from the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep\tThe first armoury was empty of weapons. Perhaps some implements of war remain in the other armoury on the eastern side of the Skarháld keep.\n3\tTalk to Tomókh in the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep\tTomókh has called for your attention inside the eastern armoury inside the Skarháld keep.\n4\tTalk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tDurin is waiting by the Skarháld stable-master for you to return with weapons from the armouries.\n5\tOne of the Zhélruka hunting parties went to the east of Skarháld.\t\n6\tTalk to the Zhélruka drake-hunter east of Skarháld\tOne of the Zhélruka hunting parties went east of Skarháld.\n7\tFind the second Zhélruka hunting-party somewhere to the north-east\tThe second Zhélruka hunting-party continued their hunt to the north-east of the first.\n8\tCollect the abandoned weapons from the slain hunting-party (total: 4)\tThe second Zhélruka hunting-party ran afoul of the drakes they sought, and now you should collect the weapons they took from Skarháld.\n9\tReturn the \"borrowed\" weapons to Durin at the stable-master in Skarháld\tDurin is waiting by the stable-master in Skarháld for you to return with the weapons the Zhélruka \"borrowed.\"\n",
[2838]="70064637\n1\tFind the Pelargir Armoury south of Sirgon's Manor, in King's Gondor\tThe Pelargir Armoury is to the south of Sirgon's Manor.\n2\tTalk to Cuguril outside the Pelargir Armoury\tThe guardswoman Cuguril stands watch outside the Pelargir Armoury.\n3\tCheck that the Armour of the Usurper remains inside the Pelargir Armoury\030Defeat pests within the Pelargir Armoury (total: 8)\tCuguril invited you to check on the Armour of the Usurper inside the Pelargir Armoury, as long as you also deal with any of the pests you might find inside.\n4\tTalk to Cuguril outside the Pelargir Armoury\tCuguril stands watch outside the Pelargir Armoury.\n5\tTalk to Legolas outside the Pelargir Armoury\tLegolas has had an idea.\n6\tConvince Legolas that you are truly angry\tLegolas has begun a dramatic argument for the benefit of the nearby onlooker, and he needs your help to show that you are truly angry. You will be most convincing if you target the Elf and use the Angry emote.\n7\tTalk to Legolas outside the Pelargir Armoury\tLegolas stands outside the Pelargir Armoury, pretending to be angry with you.\n8\tWalk by the suspicious onlooker to the south-east and see if she speaks to you\tThe suspicious onlooker is to the south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.\n9\tTalk to Aithil south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor\tThe woman Aithil is south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.\n",
[2839]="70048C39\n1\tTalk to Aragorn outside the Black Gate\tAragorn is outside the Black Gate.\n2\tTalk to Rathnor the waggon-driver\tThe waggon-driver Rathnor can be found near the Black Gate.\n3\tTalk to Ayorzén outside the Black Gate\tAyorzén is outside the Black Gate.\n4\tTalk to Hujâ at the Black Gate\030Talk to Arâm at the Black Gate\030Talk to Itli at the Black Gate\tAyorzén has given you the names of especial terrors in Mordor, and wants you to speak those names to some of the freed Nurnhoth at the Black Gate.\n5\tTalk to Ayorzén outside the Black Gate\tAyorzén is outside the Black Gate.\n6\tTalk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is outside the Black Gate.\n",
[2840]="70064872\n1\tAgree with Aithil to preserve your deception\tThe woman Aithil, south-east of the Pelargir Armoury, is convinced that you agree with the Heirs of Castamir. You should ensure she continues to believe it.\n2\tReturn to Sirgon's Manor with what you have learned\tSirgon's Manor is located to the north of the Pelargir Armoury, in King's Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Legolas inside Sirgon's Manor\030Talk to Gimli inside Sirgon's Manor\tLegolas and Gimli have come to Sirgon's Manor to await your tidings.\n4\tTalk to Faltharan in his father's manor\tFaltharan is inside his father's manor.\n5\tTravel to Amon Anglebed, the beacon outside Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor\tFaltharan told you that Amon Anglebed has been kept burning, and may be the beacon about which the skulking woman spoke.\n6\tAgree with the man and determine his loyalties\tA man stands by the beacon. Perhaps he is the contact about whom you were told, and if you agree with him he will reveal himself.\n7\tTalk to Maethon by the lit beacon, in King's Gondor\tMaethon stands by the burning beacon of Amon Anglebed, in King's Gondor.\n",
[2841]="70056ECA\n1\tFind Imák and calm him down\030Find Gílpi and calm him down\tThe brawling dwarves can be found to the north-west and up two levels from the stable-master in Skarháld.\n2\tHelp Heilar to his feet and find out what happened\tTensions run high as Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards quarrel at Skarháld.\n3\tTalk to Heilar\030Talk to Venko\tTensions run high as Stout-axes, Zhélruka, and Longbeards quarrel at Skarháld. Durin tasked you with easing these tensions, if such a thing is possible.\n4\tTalk to Imák\tImák the Stout-axe still glowers at Heilar the Longbeard. Durin asked you to ease the tensions among these dwarves, if such a thing is possible.\n5\tCollect clean mugs at Skarháld (total: 4)\tIn order to help ease the tensions among the quarrelling dwarves, you have decided to fetch four clean mugs and fill them with ale from one of the kegs at Skarháld.\n6\tUse Keg of Ale\tA keg of ale stands south of the quarrelling dwarves in Skarháld. You have gathered four (mostly) clean mugs and should now fill them from the ale-keg.\n7\tUse Keg of Ale\tA keg of ale stands south of the quarrelling dwarves in Skarháld. You have gathered four (mostly) clean mugs and should now fill them from an ale-keg.\n8\tUse Keg of Ale\tThe ale-keg ran dry after filling two of the mugs, and now you need to find another keg or risk making the dwarves' quarrel worse instead of better!\n9\tUse Keg of Ale\tYou found another ale-keg in Skarháld and can now fill the last of the mugs you collected.\n10\tBring the mugs of ale to the quarrelling dwarves in the north-west corner\tThe quarrelling dwarves are two levels up from the stable-master at Skarháld, in the north-west corner, waiting for you to return with the mugs of ale you promised.\n11\tTalk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tDurin is waiting by the stable-master in Skarháld for you to return.\n",
[2842]="70056ECB\n1\tReturn to Imák and Venko in the north-west corner, two levels up from the Skarháld stable-master\tImák and Venko can be found two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld, in the north-west corner.\n2\tTalk to Imák of the Stout-axes in Skarháld\tImák of the Stout-axes is in the north-west corner, two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld.\n3\tTalk to Venko of the Zhélruka in Skarháld\tVenko of the Zhélruka is in the north-west corner, two levels up from the stable-master in Skarháld.\n4\tTalk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tDurin is waiting by the Skarháld stable-master to hear that Imák and Venko will go in search of the raiding-party in the Wells of Langflood.\n5\tTalk to Glóin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tGlóin has made it known he wishes to speak with you and Durin at the stable-master in Skarháld.\n6\tCollect the bag of foodstuffs in Skarháld, two levels up\030Collect the bag of climbing gear in Skarháld, three levels up\030Collect the bag of camping gear in Skarháld, two levels up\tA bag of foodstuffs can be found two levels above the Skarháld stable-master. Climbing gear can be found three levels above the Skarháld stable-master Flint and camping supplies can be found two levels above the Skarháld stable-master.\n7\tBring the supplies to Glóin by the stable-master at Skarháld\tGlóin is by the stable-master in Skarháld.\n8\tTalk to Durin by the stable-master in Skarháld\tDurin is by the stable-master in Skarháld.\n9\tFind your travelling companions to the west of Skarháld, at the pass to the Wells of Langflood east and south of the broken Rushgate\tThe way to the Wells of Langflood from the Grey Mountains is west of Skarháld, accessible by a narrow pass in the southern cliffs east of the broken Rushgate.\n10\tTalk to Glóin by the path leading into Misthallow\tGlóin is at the entrance to the pass that leads to the Wells of Langflood from the Grey Mountains, east and south of the broken Rushgate.\n",
[2843]="700649B6\n1\tCollect Maethon's parchments from the crate outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed\tMaethon stashed a number of parchments to distribute on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir in a crate outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed, to the north-east.\n2\tResidents of Ost Anglebed can be found throughout the city if you wish to hand out the parchments, or you can burn Maethon's parchments in the nearby brazier.\t\n3\tResidents of Ost Anglebed can be found throughout the city if you wish to hand out the parchments, or you can burn Maethon's parchments in the nearby brazier.\t\n4\tReturn to Maethon at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed\tMaethon will want to hear about your efforts on behalf of the Heirs of Castamir. He should still be at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed.\n5\tTalk to Ladben at the lit beacon of Amon Anglebed\tA guardsman of Ost Anglebed, Ladben, stands by the lit beacon.\n6\tPick up the beacon oil at Amon Anglebed\tLadben asked you to bring the container of beacon oil to Halwen for safekeeping. Halwen keeps watch over the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed.\n7\tTalk to Maethon by the stairs\tMaethon stands beside the stairs to the Hall of Ost Anglebed, calling for you in hushed tones.\n8\tWait for Maethon to leave before you begin his errand\tMaethon makes himself scarce so you can accomplish his goal.\n9\tTalk to Halwen by the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed\tHalwen stands by the supplies near the north-east fountain in Ost Anglebed.\n10\tHalwen believed your story that Ladben needs a barrel of weapons, and she told you to take one from the other side of the fountain. She warned you that there is a barrel of rusty weapons there as well, so be careful not to bring Ladben weapons of poor quality.\t\n11\tTalk to Maethon below the cliff south of the eastern entrance of Ost Anglebed\tMaethon stands below the cliff south of the eastern entrance to Ost Anglebed.\n",
[2844]="700649B9\n1\tFind the entrance to the dwelling in the northern half of Linhir where supporters of the Heirs of Castamir intend to meet\tMaethon described the location where the supporters of the Heirs of Castamir intend to meet. It is a dwelling in the northern half of the city of Linhir, opposite a fountain and with a bronze door.\n2\tEnter the building by the fountain in the northern half of Linhir and attend the meeting\tYou should enter the building by the fountain in the northern half of Linhir and attend the meeting.\n3\tTalk to Nakási outside Linhir\tNakási is outside Linhir, south of the eastern entrance.\n4\tTalk to the gossipmonger inside the eastern entrance to Linhir\tThe Linhir gossipmonger has news, and can be found just inside the eastern entrance to Linhir, in King's Gondor.\n",
[2845]="7006B58B\n1\tTalk to Rahâzi outside the grove of Arwáth and return with her to Iridír\tRahâzi is outside the grove of Arwáth, preparing to return to Iridír.\n2\tTalk to Khôltekh within Iridír\tKhôltekh stands within the village of Iridír, studying the people nearby with interest.\n3\tReturn to Girhâzi in her lodge within Iridír\tGirhâzi is inside her lodge within Iridír.\n4\tTalk to Girhâzi in her lodge within Iridír\tGirhâzi is in her lodge within Iridír.\n",
[2846]="7006B590\n1\tTalk to Khôltekh in Iridír\030Talk to Rothog in Iridír\030Talk to Belondor in Iridír\030Talk to Corudan in Iridír\030Talk to Sigileth in Iridír\tGirhâzi gave a number of tasks to your travelling companions for them to complete in order to earn the trust of her people, and to learn valuable information that will benefit your own mission in Ambarûl.\n2\tScout the eastern side of the Wrackwade in the camp of Sûru to the south\030Join Rothog outside the Ordâkhai camp at Eshadur\030Join Khôltekh outside the brigand camp of Bidrokh-nûn\030Scout the road from Ambarûl to Urash Dâr, south-east of Iridír\030Defeat brigands in Ambarûl (total: 6)\030Defeat Ordâkhai in Ambarûl (total: 6)\030Collect stingers from usan-kûni scorpions in Ambarûl (total: 4)\tYour companions have been given a number of places to scout and enemies to defeat there: at the eastern side of the Wrackwade in the camp of Sûru, an Ordâkhai camp at Eshadur across the river, a brigand camp to the south-east, and the road to Urash Dâr.\n3\tBring the scorpion stingers to Girhâzi in Iridír\tGirhâzi waits for your successful return in Iridír.\n",
[2847]="7006B591\n1\tTalk to Rahâzi on the eastern side of the lodge in Iridír\tRahâzi is on the eastern side of her mother's lodge in Iridír.\n2\tOffer a pillow to Khôltekh\030Offer a pillow to Rothog\030Offer a pillow to Corudan\030Offer a pillow to Belondor\030Offer a pillow to Sigileth\tYour companions throughout the village of Iridír may welcome the gift of pillows, or they may not.\n3\tPrepare your sleeping mat on the western side of the lodge in the village of Iridír\tYour task complete, you can now rest for the night in the village of Iridír. Sleeping mats for this purpose can be found on the western side of the lodge.\n4\tRest for the night on your sleeping mat in the lodge within Iridír\tYour sleeping mat awaits on the western side of the lodge in the village of Iridír.\n5\tTalk to Corudan at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge\tYour own sleep disturbed by troubling dreams, you hope that your companions are feeling more rested than you. They can be found at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge.\n6\tTalk to Sigileth at the entrance of Iridír\tYour own sleep disturbed by troubling dreams, you hope that your companions are feeling more rested than you. They can be found at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge.\n7\tTalk to Sirgon at the entrance of Iridír\tYour own sleep disturbed by troubled dreams, you hope that your companions are feeling more rested than you. They can be found at the entrance of Iridír to the north of the lodge.\n",
[2848]="7005275D\n1\tTalk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld\tDurin is on the upper level of Skarháld, waiting to speak with you following Karazgar's defeat.\n2\tTalk to King Thranduil at his throne in Felegoth\tKing Thranduil is in the throne room of Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen.\n3\tMake your way through Eryn Lasgalen to the Forest Gate in the west\tThe Forest Gate is located on the western edge of Eryn Lasgalen, along the forest road.\n4\tTalk to Gandalf at the Forest Gate in Eryn Lasgalen\tGandalf stands at the Forest Gate on the western edge of Eryn Lasgalen, waiting to speak with you.\n5\tMake your way to the entrance of the Beorninghús south-west of the Forest Gate\tThe Beorninghús is located in the Beorning-lands, south-west of the Forest Gate.\n6\tTalk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús\tGrimbeorn stands at the Beorninghús.\n",
})
